  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Purpose" xml:space="preserve"><value>Shows how ready the company is for a recall: open cases, the last drill against its target, lot coverage of outbound movements, untraceable outbound movements and returns of open cases.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Audience" xml:space="preserve"><value>Quality (recall owner), quality system administrator and management (read-only).</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Step1Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose the company</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Step1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Every figure on this page belongs to the selected company only.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Step2Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Read the cards</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Step2" xml:space="preserve"><value>A red “Target exceeded” on the last drill or a non-zero untraceable count needs attention.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Step3Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Watch the drill history</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLDASHBOARD.Step3" xml:space="preserve"><value>The chart shows the last 12 completed drills against the target line; the band above warns when the last drill is too old.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Purpose" xml:space="preserve"><value>Traces a lot through the whole genealogy, backward to its inputs and forward to stock, shipments and customers, and shows the gaps where a lot cannot prove where goods went.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Audience" xml:space="preserve"><value>Quality (recall owner) and the quality system administrator.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Step1Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pick the lot</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Step1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Search the lot number and choose the direction: backward, forward or both.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Step2Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Read the tree or the table</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Step2" xml:space="preserve"><value>Both views show the same nodes. Red rows are trace gaps; another company’s activity appears only as a count.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Step3Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Export or open a case</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Step3" xml:space="preserve"><value>“Download CSV” gives the same rows; “Open a recall case with this scope” opens a draft case from this trace.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLTRACE.Immediate" xml:space="preserve"><value>Opening a case creates a draft immediately; nothing is blocked until its scope is approved.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLCASES.Purpose" xml:space="preserve"><value>Lists the company’s real recall cases and drills together, newest first, with their status and progress.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLCASES.Audience" xml:space="preserve"><value>Everyone who follows recalls: quality, warehouse, commercial and management.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLCASES.Step1Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Filter the list</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLCASES.Step1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use type, status, class, product and the opening date. A class filter shows real cases only.</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLCASES.Step2Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tell drills apart</value></data>
  <data name="Help.RECALLCASES.Step2" xml:space="preserve"><value>A drill row says “Drill”, shows its result and duration, and has no class or level.</value></data>
